#: ui_dialogs.py:6255
msgid ""
"\"Preview before saving\" shows the nest and the material used before "
"anything is written. Save Files writes; Adjust goes back. One material at"
" a time."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6259
msgid "Spreads one pad list over several scraps."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6261
msgid "Tick Scrap Mode and one material."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6262
msgid "Enter this scrap's size, or draw or capture its shape."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6263
msgid ""
"Generate or Frame & Cut. What fits is cut; the rest waits for the next "
"scrap."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6264
msgid "Between scraps keep the shape, unload it, or Re-capture from camera."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6266
msgid ""
"The progress window shows what is left, what is on this scrap and what is"
" done. A scrap counts once its file is written or its cut has finished."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6268
msgid "You can edit the pad list during a session; it counts from the next scrap."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6269
msgid "Files are named _scrap1, _scrap2 and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6272
msgid ""
"Small discs look alike once cut. Labeled Zones cuts each size in its own "
"block with the size engraved on the border, on the waste. Sizing Rules > "
"Lesser-used settings; off by default; set the size range."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6276
msgid "Zones use more material than a free nest."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6277
msgid ""
"A size that cannot get its block is left uncut and reported, never cut "
"unlabeled."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6278
msgid ""
"A \"max\" size inside the zone range is refused. A \"max\" size outside "
"it fills in around the blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6280
msgid "Zones are off in Scrap Mode."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6283
msgid ""
"Engraves where the felt sits on a leather pad (four lines, a circle, or "
"both), so a pad with no center hole can be centered by eye. Sizing Rules "
"> Lesser-used settings; set the size range."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6286
msgid ""
"The marks belong on the side the felt touches: cut the leather flesh "
"(fuzzy) side up when you use them."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6288
msgid ""
"SVG puts them on their own layer (Leather locator in Layer Colors) for "
"their own power in LightBurn. G-code engraves them at the leather "
"engraving settings."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6293
msgid ""
"A fifth material: a ring of double-sided tape per pad, for sticking a "
"silicone wrap to the back of the card. Switch it on in Sizing Rules > "
"Lesser-used settings, then tick Adhesive rings."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6297
msgid ""
"The outer edge is the card disc; the ring is as wide as the leather wrap "
"for that size. Wrap clearance (mm, plus or minus) makes it wider or "
"narrower."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6299
msgid ""
"The pad size is cut as single-line digits in the hole, on the piece that "
"drops out, or just under the ring when the hole is too small."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6301
msgid "Pads of 9.5 mm and under are solid discs, with the number under them."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6302
msgid ""
"SVG: one layer for ring and number. G-code cuts the number, the inside, "
"then the outside, at the ring's cut settings."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6304
msgid ""
"The laser defaults are a starting point, not tested values. Dial them in "
"on your tape with Tooling > Speed & Power Test."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6307
msgid "Engraving"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6308
msgid ""
"Each disc is engraved with its pad size. Font sizes and placement are in "
"Sizing Rules, Universal or Per Size Range."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6310
msgid ""
"out: from the cut edge. mid: halfway between hole and edge. int: from the"
" center hole."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6312
msgid ""
"Darted leather: measure \"out\" from the dart valley puts the number just"
" inside the darts. A dart tip always sits over the number."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6314
msgid ""
"A number too big for its disc moves toward the center, then shrinks. If "
"the font is over 80 percent of the disc radius it is left off, with a "
"warning first."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6318
msgid "G-code Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6319
msgid ""
"Options > G-code Settings... holds speed, power and passes for each "
"material and each step: engraving, center hole, outer cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6321
msgid ""
"Engraving mode: Line (single stroke) or Filled. Fill density and overscan"
" apply to Filled."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6323
msgid ""
"Kerf width: enter the full measured kerf (LightBurn asks for half). The "
"app compensates every cut. Measure it with Tooling > Kerf Test."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6325
msgid ""
"Air assist per step, return-to-home speed, and Cut grouping: by layer "
"(all engravings, all holes, all cuts) or by pad."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6327
msgid "Each material has its own presets: Load, Save, Rename, Delete."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6328
msgid "Test speeds and powers on the material you will really cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6330
msgid "Layer Colors"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6331
msgid ""
"Options > Layer Colors... sets the LightBurn color layer for each step. "
"SVG only. Lesser-used settings > Export Settings has a compatibility mode"
" (unitless SVG) for older software."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6335 ui_dialogs.py:7032
msgid "Job History"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6336
msgid ""
"File > Job History... lists the last 300 jobs that were written or sent "
"to the laser, newest first."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6338
msgid ""
"\"Load into Pad Maker\" puts a job's pad list, materials, sheet, center "
"hole and filename back in the form. Sizing rules, G-code settings and "
"shapes are left as they are."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6341
msgid "A stopped or errored laser run is marked *. Scrap Mode logs each scrap."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6342
msgid "Tooling jobs are listed by tool and cannot be loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6344
msgid "Pad presets"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6345
msgid ""
"Save as Preset keeps the pad list in a library; pick it from the dropdown"
" to load it. Delete Preset removes it."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6347
msgid "File > Import Matt's Pad Sets downloads Matt's sets from stohrermusic.com."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6350
msgid "Getting a job to the laser"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6352
msgid "Three ways"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6354
msgid "SD card: save the G-code to the card and run it on the laser."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6355
msgid "LightBurn: Generate SVG and set speed and power there."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6356
msgid "Frame & Cut: the app sends it over USB."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6358
msgid "G-code or SVG?"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6359
msgid ""
"A G-code file carries its own speeds and powers, the ones set in this "
"app. Send it to the laser as it is, on an SD card or with Frame & Cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6361
msgid ""
"LightBurn ignores those values when it imports G-code, so for LightBurn "
"use Generate SVG and set speed and power there."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6364
msgid "Machine integration"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6366
msgid ""
"File > Feature Set..., under Experimental / In Progress: tick \"Machine "
"menu (direct Falcon serial control)\". Restart."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6368
msgid ""
"Connect the laser by USB, before or after starting the app. Frame & Cut "
"appears within seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6371
msgid ""
"Options > Machine (Pad Maker): Home Laser, Test Connection, Clear Errors,"
" Reset Falcon, Camera Calibration, Camera-Polygon Inset Margin, Framing "
"Power (dim, per material)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6377
msgid "Click Frame & Cut, check the preview, Continue →."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6378
msgid "Jog to the material's visible bottom-left corner, even on a tilted scrap."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6379
msgid ""
"Click Start Frame →. It asks \"Is the lid closed?\": framing turns the "
"laser on, low power is still power, and an open lid alarms the machine."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6381
msgid "It traces the outline at low power; jog between passes if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6382
msgid "Click \"Looks Good — Cut!\"."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6384
msgid "Framing is a live laser: keep your hands out of the bed."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6385
msgid "Stop is a soft reset. No calibration needed."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6387
msgid "Camera"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6388
msgid "Optional. Options > Machine > Camera Calibration..., done once:"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6390
msgid "Secure basswood, home, jog to mid-bed, Frame, then Engrave."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6391
msgid ""
"Capture the card untouched first, click Done with references, then move "
"it for the rest of the 12."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6393
msgid ""
"This unlocks \"Get from camera\", the shape dialog's live overlay, Try "
"Auto Locate, Re-capture from camera and \"Live camera preview\"."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6395
msgid ""
"Live camera preview closes while another window needs the camera and "
"returns with the next Frame & Cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6397
msgid ""
"\"Camera #1 could not be opened; showing camera #2.\": the saved camera "
"is gone. Switch camera saves the other one."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6401
msgid "Windows: \"Eject SD card after G-code export\" ejects it after writing."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6405
msgid ""
"Laser files for the die holders and die inserts you assemble pads in, "
"plus a few shop tools. Pick a tool with its button, fill it in, then "
"Generate SVG, Generate G-code or Frame & Cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6408
msgid ""
"The die inserts and die holders follow Phil Noy's pad-making method, "
"which he shares freely: every die insert is engraved \"NOY\" and every "
"holder ring \"DESIGNED BY PHIL NOY\"."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6411
msgid "noysaxophonesupplies.com"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6415
msgid "An acrylic ring for each pad size; the pad is assembled in its hole."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6416
msgid "Pads 7.0 to 39.5 mm get a 50 mm ring, 40.0 to 60.0 mm a 70 mm ring."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6417
msgid ""
"Enter sizes (7, 8.5, 25) or ranges (15-30, by Step), or click Full Set "
"(S), Full Set (L) or Full Set (All)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6419
msgid ""
"\"Engrave size on ring\" numbers the ring. \"Engrave size on cutout\" "
"numbers the disc that drops out with its real size."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6421
msgid "Dies nest in rows from the sheet's bottom-left corner, largest first."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6422
msgid ""
"The cutout discs make handy pad cup tools. For an exact diameter, use the"
" Pad Maker's Exact size (SVG only)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6426
msgid ""
"A stack of 85 mm acrylic discs cemented together for good: a solid "
"bottom, a magnet disc (6.5 mm hole), two or three pin discs (3.5 mm "
"holes) and a retaining ring."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6429
msgid ""
"Pick 5 or 6 layers, and Small (50 mm dies), Large (70 mm) or Both, two "
"complete holders on one sheet."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6431
msgid "If the pieces don't fit the sheet, it says the smallest sheet that works."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6434
msgid ""
"A stacking rack for dies, 230 x 330 mm. Cut three upper plates and one "
"lower, line up the four 1/8 in corner holes on pins and glue the stack; a"
" book press clamps it nicely."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6437
msgid ""
"Pick basswood, acrylic or cork and the sheet. G-code cuts every slot and "
"hole before the plate's edge; the sheet must be at least 234 x 334 mm."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6439
msgid "The SVG is the bare drawing, for LightBurn."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6442
msgid "Kerf is the full width the beam removes. Measure it for each material:"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6445
msgid "Pick the material and cut the test: three discs, 10, 20 and 30 mm."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6446
msgid "Pop the discs out and measure each hole and disc with calipers."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6447
msgid "Kerf = hole diameter minus disc diameter."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6448
msgid ""
"Enter that full kerf in G-code Settings (LightBurn asks for half). The "
"app compensates every cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6451
msgid ""
"It cuts at the material's settings; untick \"Use existing G-code settings"
" for this material\" to try others."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6455
msgid ""
"Beta. Cuts small discs, each at its own speed, power and passes and "
"engraved with an ID; a legend file lists them. Keep the settings of the "
"discs that came free cleanly without scorching."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6458
msgid "\"Apply material defaults\" fills the fields from the material."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6459
msgid ""
"Tick Sweep on Speed, Power or Passes to test Stops values from Start to "
"End; untick to hold one value."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6461
msgid "\"Also test with air off\" runs half the discs without air."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6462
msgid ""
"Keep the engraving readable: the IDs are the point. A hole diameter above"
" 0 makes washers, for shim stock."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6464
msgid "G-code only: an SVG would lose each disc's settings."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6465 ui_dialogs.py:6750
msgid "Test on the material you will really cut."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6468
msgid ""
"3D-printable 1.75 in square spacers with their thickness on top; stack "
"them to set press depth. A half-step set (3.0 to 4.5 mm), a quarter-step "
"set (3.25 to 4.25 mm) and a rack. Print in PLA or PETG."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6473
msgid ""
"A crescent glued into the mouthpiece side of a tonehole covers part of it"
" and flattens that note. Enter the tonehole ID and the percent of its "
"open area to cover."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6477
msgid ""
"Inner edge: \"Match tonehole curve\" is the classic crescent; flatter is "
"shorter and wider, rounder longer and thinner. The area stays the same."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6479
msgid ""
"For several, set each up with a quantity and click Add to list. Generate "
"makes the list, or the fields when it is empty. The SVG numbers each part"
" on the scrap."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6482
msgid ""
"G-code cuts the chosen material (cork by default) half a kerf outside the"
" outline, so the part comes out at size."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6484
msgid ""
"The SVG has no kerf compensation; set it in LightBurn. Generate STL "
"prints it at the thickness entered."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6488
msgid ""
"Tick Scrap Mode on Die Inserts to spread a set over several sheets: each "
"Generate fills one sheet, a window tracks what is left, and files are "
"named _scrap1, _scrap2."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6493
msgid ""
"Every tool that writes G-code has Frame & Cut beside Generate G-code. It "
"sends the same job the file would hold, the same way as on the Pad Maker."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6495
msgid "Jog to the sheet's bottom-left corner."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6496
msgid "Speed & Power Test asks where to save its legend before the laser moves."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6497
msgid ""
"In Scrap Mode each click cuts one sheet; a sheet counts only once its cut"
" has finished."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6500
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6501
msgid ""
"Options > Settings...: speed, power, passes, kerf and air for acrylic, "
"basswood and cork, and the die engraving options (line or filled, font "
"sizes, ring placement)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6504
msgid ""
"Die inserts and holders use the acrylic settings. Defaults suit a Falcon2"
" Pro 40W on 3 mm acrylic and basswood; adjust for your laser."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6506
msgid "The basswood settings also engrave the camera calibration card."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6507
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Cork: the default cut was tested at 1000 mm/min and 30 % on 3/32 in cork "
"with a 40 W laser. The kerf is not measured (0) and the engraving is not "
"set (0 and 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6510
msgid ""
"While cork's engraving is not set, nothing is engraved on cork, and the "
"app says so before it cuts."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6515
msgid ""
"Record and compare key heights for different saxophones, in libraries you"
" can share."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6517
msgid "Options > Layout Options... chooses which keys are shown."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6518
msgid ""
"File > Import Matt's Key Heights downloads Matt's sets from "
"stohrermusic.com."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6522
msgid ""
"Pick the maker and type the serial number to estimate the year it was "
"made."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6526
msgid "Thread specifications for screws and rods, by saxophone model."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6527
msgid "File > Import Matt's Specs downloads the latest from stohrermusic.com."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6531
msgid ""
"A strobe tuner: one wheel per note, one ring per octave. It runs while "
"the tab is open."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6533
msgid ""
"Frozen pattern: in tune. Drifting right: sharp. Left: flat. The faster "
"the drift, the further off."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6535
msgid "Several wheels move at once: those are the harmonics in your sound."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6536
msgid "The VU meter at the bottom shows the note and how many cents off it is."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6538
msgid "Controls"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6539
msgid "DISP: SENS (how loud a sound must be), BRIGHT, FPS (60, 90 or 120)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6540
msgid "PITCH: A= reference (440 Hz by default), KEY transposition (C, Bb, Eb, F)."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6541
msgid ""
"BIAS: NOTE brightens the played octave's ring; OCT. boosts the strongest "
"ring."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6542
msgid ""
"Options > Settings...: backlight and faceplate colors, frame-rate "
"readout. Options > Input Device... picks the microphone."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6545
msgid "Microphone"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6546
msgid ""
"A good mic matters most on low notes. A USB condenser such as the Audio-"
"Technica AT2020 USB works well, as does any condenser through an audio "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6549
msgid ""
"Built-in laptop mics manage basic tuning but struggle low down. Bluetooth"
" headset mics do not work: their sample rate is too low."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6552 ui_dialogs.py:6686
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6553
msgid ""
"Each wheel turns at the difference between the sound and its note, from "
"real analysis of the audio, not a simulation."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6555
msgid ""
"It draws on the graphics card where it can (60 to 120 fps) and falls back"
" to a slower drawing mode where it can't."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6560
msgid ""
"A harmonic analyzer: it finds the note you play and measures each "
"harmonic up to the 20th. Every reading is the whole chain at once: "
"player, horn, mouthpiece, reed, mic and room."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6563
msgid ""
"So it measures change, not gear. Change one thing at a time and compare. "
"Mouthpiece, player and mic routinely outweigh horn-to-horn differences; "
"compare your setups with your other setups."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6567
msgid "Two ways to use it"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6568
msgid ""
"Live: watch the spectrum while you play to see how air, embouchure and "
"voicing change the sound."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6570
msgid ""
"Over time: record a session, change one thing, record another, and "
"compare. The thing you changed is the difference: a mouthpiece, a mic, a "
"horn, or you on another day."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6573
msgid "Be skeptical of strong conclusions from small samples."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6575
msgid "Before you capture"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6576
msgid ""
"You need a preset: File > Presets.... Make, Model, Player, Mouthpiece, "
"Mic Type and Mic Model are required. More fields can be switched on in "
"Options > Settings... > Analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6579
msgid "The SAX selector sets the transposition and is saved with the preset."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6580
msgid ""
"A condenser mic (such as an AT2020 USB) gives the fullest picture. Ribbon"
" and dynamic mics dull the upper harmonics; the Analyze tool warns when "
"mic types differ."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6583
msgid "Laptop mics are not suitable. Bluetooth headset mics do not work."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6585
msgid "Mic placement"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6586
msgid ""
"2 to 3 feet (60 to 90 cm) from the bell, slightly off-axis, in a quiet "
"room. Closer than a foot exaggerates the low harmonics."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6588
msgid ""
"Mic position matters more than almost anything: a few inches between "
"takes can shift complexity 10 to 20 percent. Use a stand at a fixed spot,"
" and note it in the Mic Position field."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6592
msgid "Capturing"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6594
msgid "Click Capture and pick or create a preset."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6595
msgid "Play. Hold a note about a second and it is captured; move on to the next."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6596
msgid ""
"Click Stop. A summary shows which notes you covered and where the gaps "
"are."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6598
msgid "Capture at least 8 different notes; more is better."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6599
msgid ""
"Calibration mode walks you up a chromatic scale, 5 seconds per note. File"
" > Presets... > Import Audio File... analyzes a WAV."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6601
msgid "Sessions are dated and saved automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6603
msgid "Display"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6604
msgid "Spectrum or Bars view, with Linear (true ratios) or dB scale."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6605
msgid ""
"The intonation gauge shows cents flat or sharp; the IN TUNE lamp lights "
"within 4 cents."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6607
msgid ""
"Overlay on Spectrum (from the Analyze tool) shows a stored preset as blue"
" ghost bars behind the live spectrum, note by note."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6610
msgid "Analyze"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6611
msgid ""
"File > Analyze... shows what differs between presets: not which is "
"better, but what changed and where."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6613
msgid "Filter the picker by horn type, player, mouthpiece and mic type."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6614
msgid ""
"One preset: its descriptors and harmonic curve. Two: side by side with a "
"Difference chart. Three or more: the spread across the group."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6616
msgid ""
"Horn Average or Per-Note shows whether a difference is everywhere or in "
"one register."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6618
msgid "Percentiles rank each preset against all presets of the same sax type."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6619
msgid ""
"Click a legend label or chart line for that preset's details. Back "
"returns to the picker."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6621
msgid ""
"The table shows each preset's mic type and rolloff, and notes when mics "
"differ."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6624
msgid "Descriptors"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6625
msgid ""
"Most useful as differences between two presets, where mic and room "
"effects cancel. Choose which are shown in Options > Settings... > "
"Analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6627
msgid ""
"Warmth (Thin to Warm): the strength of the 2nd harmonic. Not the same as "
"dark: a sound can be warm and bright, or thin and dark."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6629
msgid ""
"Some setups, metal mouthpieces played hard especially, make the 2nd "
"harmonic louder than the fundamental. Warmth reads these as moderately "
"warm; this part of the formula may change."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6632
msgid ""
"Harmonic Complexity (Pure to Complex): how evenly the energy spreads over"
" the harmonics."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6634
msgid ""
"Even/Odd Ratio: even against odd harmonics, round against edgy. The most "
"consistent across recording conditions. On by default."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6636
msgid ""
"Rolloff Shape (Smooth to Peaked): bumps where harmonics stick out. Off by"
" default."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6638
msgid ""
"Evenness (Variable to Even): how alike the character is across the range."
" Needs at least 5 notes."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6641
msgid "Character Map"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6642
msgid ""
"Plots Warmth against Harmonic Complexity, so each preset sits in one of "
"four corners: warm and bright, warm and dark, thin and bright, thin and "
"dark. All four are real characters."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6645
msgid ""
"Warmth comes from how the chamber and reed couple to the fundamental, "
"brightness from the reed's buzz on the tip rail, so they move "
"independently."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6647
msgid ""
"H4-H5 mean and Rolloff are offered as other axes, but they tend to follow"
" Warmth."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6648
msgid ""
"Compare within one sax type: lower horns read warmer and brighter "
"whatever the mouthpiece. It warns before mixing types."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6651
msgid "Reading the differences"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6652
msgid ""
"H1 to H4: mostly the bore; the least change in player and mouthpiece "
"swaps."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6653
msgid "H7 to H13: where neck and mouthpiece swaps show most."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6654
msgid "H3 to H12 all together: usually mouthpiece or player."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6655
msgid ""
"Two takes of one setup ten minutes apart differed by 1 to 3 percent on "
"descriptors and about 0.3 dB/H on rolloff. Smaller differences are "
"probably noise."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6658
msgid ""
"These are observed patterns, not laws. Same-player comparisons isolate "
"equipment best."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6661
msgid "Recording quality"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6662
msgid ""
"Rolloff, how fast the upper harmonics fade, shows how much your recording"
" catches:"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6664
msgid "1.0 to 2.0 dB/H: condenser, close. Full detail."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6665
msgid "2.0 to 2.5 dB/H: good mic, further away or a lively room."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6666
msgid ""
"Over 2.5 dB/H: ribbon, dynamic, built-in or distant mic. The app warns "
"after the first few captures."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6669
msgid "Presets and data"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6670
msgid ""
"Mutate Preset copies a preset with its fields filled in, so you can "
"change one thing and save it as new."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6672
msgid ""
"Sandbox mode (Options > Settings... > Analysis) relaxes the required "
"fields for other instruments and experiments. Sandbox presets are marked "
"in amber."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6675
msgid ""
"A preset's report shows its sessions over time, with the change from each"
" to the next and a per-note breakdown."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6677
msgid "File > Transfer Data exports or imports the preset library."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6679
msgid "WAV recording"
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6680
msgid ""
"On by default; the first capture asks for a folder. At the end of a "
"session the recording is analyzed again, more strictly than live, and "
"that better result is what is stored."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6683
msgid ""
"Turn it off, or delete each WAV after analysis, in Options > Settings... "
"> General."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6684
msgid ""
"Keep the WAVs to listen back, share, or re-analyze with better tools "
"later."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6687
msgid ""
"Harmonics are measured in dB against the fundamental, so volume and mic "
"gain drop out. Below -60 dB counts as noise."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6689
msgid "The first tenth of a second of each note, the attack, is skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6690
msgid ""
"The detector checks whether a loud peak is a harmonic of a lower note, "
"which keeps it from reading the wrong octave."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6692
msgid ""
"Notes are averaged first, then the notes together, so many captures of "
"one register don't outweigh the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6694
msgid ""
"Only raw measurements are stored. Descriptors are worked out fresh each "
"time, so improvements apply to old captures too."
msgstr ""

#: ui_dialogs.py:6698
